#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD9725 expect=skipped domain=PP
#note "The discriminator that keeps the family from double-reporting: BOTH interval columns EXIST (blank on the interval-test row), so Requirements.Variables.None [--STINT, --ENINT] skips this sister with a reason naming the first present column, and the parent FDA-SD1348 owns the case -- its All gate is satisfied and it reports row 1 with its location."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset PP class=FINDINGS label="Pharmacokinetics Parameters"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col PPSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col PPTESTCD type=Char label="Parameter Short Name"
col PPTEST   type=Char label="Parameter Name"
col PPSTINT  type=Char label="Planned Start of Assessment Interval"
col PPENINT  type=Char label="Planned End of Assessment Interval"
---
S1 | PP | 001 | 1 | AUCINT | AUC from T1 to T2 |  |
